        "--groups",
        "normal,frozen_core",
        "--resamples",
        "100",
        "--help"
      ],
      "exit_code": 0,
      "stdout": "Usage: coimnet examples run attribution [--task avoid_obstacles] [--seeds 1,2,3] [--episodes 1] [--hidden 4] [--recurrent 1] [--eval 1] [--groups all|normal,frozen_core,...] [--learning-rate 0.05] [--resamples 100] [--interval 0.95] [--out FILE]\nRuns the synthetic two-dimensional navigation attribution fixture. Reports contain every selected group and seed, paired bootstrap comparisons, and the fixed conclusion. Indented JSON goes to --out, or stdout when omitted; the summary goes to stdout with --out and stderr otherwise.\nGroups:\n  normal: trains core weights and both encoder and readout.\n  frozen_core: fixes core weights at initialization and trains encoder and readout.\n  core_only: fixes an identity encoder and an identity readout that reads only action nodes, and trains only core weights.\n  generic_matched: uniformly samples unique edges between the same node groups with the same edge count, then trains like normal.\n  rewired: performs degree-preserving double-edge swaps on the hidden recurrent block, then trains like normal.\n  ablated_retrained: removes the core and retrains encoder and readout from scratch.\n  capacity_matched_modulator: adds readout capacity sized to the MOD-10 controller and otherwise trains like normal.\nComparison: paired bootstrap against normal on the unseen-map success rate and expert agreement, using same-seed differences. When core_only does not learn, the report attaches the troubleshooting checks; the periphery is never enlarged. The only conclusion is the fixed sentence: A drop after freezing or removing the core shows dependence on it, not that the original wiring is superior.\nEach config.env contains the effective environment values after defaults; config_hash is SHA-256 of that reported config.\nExample: coimnet examples run attribution --task avoid_obstacles --seeds 1,2,3 --out attribution.json\nErrors: invalid --task, --seeds, --episodes, --hidden, --recurrent, --eval, --groups, --learning-rate, --resamples or --interval; an existing --out, positional arguments, cancellation or output failure. Usage errors exit with status 1. Failed runs still emit the full report and return a nonzero status.\nOptions and their defaults:\n  -episodes int\n    \ttraining episodes per seed (1..10000) (default 60)\n  -eval int\n    \tevaluation episodes per seed (1..1000) (default 20)\n  -groups string\n    \tgroups to run: all or a comma-separated subset including normal (default \"all\")\n  -hidden int\n    \thidden units (4..128) (default 16)\n  -interval float\n    \tpaired bootstrap confidence interval (0..1) (default 0.95)\n  -learning-rate float\n    \tlearning rate (default 0.05)\n  -out string\n    \tnew report JSON file; an existing path is never overwritten (default: stdout)\n  -recurrent int\n    \trecurrent hidden units (1..hidden) (default 4)\n  -resamples int\n    \tpaired bootstrap resamples (at least 100) (default 1000)\n  -seeds string\n    \tcomma-separated distinct seeds, at least three (default \"1,2,3\")\n  -task string\n    \tnavigation task: avoid_obstacles, remember_goal, adapt_after_change or language_goal (default \"avoid_obstacles\")\n",
      "stderr": ""
    },
