      ],
      "exit_code": 0,
      "stdout": "Usage: coimnet examples run continual-matrix --out FILE [--seeds 7,42,123] [--budget 20] [--episodes 16] [--chemistry]\nBuilds the fixed two-task fixture, task A (delay 2, channel 0) and task B (delay 3, channel 1), on the three-neuron delayed-core individual and runs the continual stages train A, train B and rule-change A, where the rule change negates the gain of task A. Every seed trains its own individual; each stage is scored on both tasks with evaluation episodes the training never sees. A preregistered paired bootstrap compares every last-stage cell against the same seeds' independent re-initialized control. The report is written as indented JSON to a new --out file and a one-line summary goes to stdout.\n--chemistry adds the hypothesized octopamine layer, freezes it during evaluation and records every cell re-scored under a switched concentration.\nExample: coimnet examples run continual-matrix --chemistry --out continual-matrix.json\nErrors: missing --out, an existing --out path, fewer than three seeds or duplicate seeds, an unparsable seed, a budget outside 0..100000, episodes outside 1..10000, cancellation or output failure. Usage errors exit with status 1 and name the flag.\nOptions and their defaults:\n  -budget uint\n    \ttraining episodes per train_task stage (0..100000) (default 20)\n  -chemistry\n    \tenable the chemistry layer and re-score every cell under a switched chemical state\n  -episodes int\n    \tevaluation episodes per cell (1..10000) (default 16)\n  -out string\n    \tnew continual matrix report JSON file; an existing path is never overwritten (required)\n  -seeds string\n    \tcomma-separated deterministic seeds, at least three, no duplicates (default \"7,42,123\")\n",
      "stderr": ""
    }
